Usage: parallel-cli search [OPTIONS] [OBJECTIVE]

  Search the web using Parallel's AI-powered search.

  OBJECTIVE is a natural language description of what you're looking for. You
  can also pass specific keyword queries with --query. At least one of
  OBJECTIVE or --query is required. Use "-" as OBJECTIVE to read from stdin.

Options:
  -q, --query TEXT                Keyword search query (can be repeated)
  --mode [turbo|fast|basic|advanced|one-shot|agentic]
                                  Search mode: turbo (fastest), fast (high
                                  quality within ~1s), basic, or advanced
                                  (highest quality; one-shot → basic, agentic
                                  → advanced)  [default: basic]
  --max-results INTEGER           Maximum results (defaults to server-side
                                  default of 10)
  --include-domains TEXT          Only search these domains (comma-separated
                                  or repeated)
  --exclude-domains TEXT          Exclude these domains (comma-separated or
                                  repeated)
  --after-date TEXT               Only results after this date (YYYY-MM-DD)
  --excerpt-max-chars-per-result INTEGER
                                  Max characters per result for excerpts (min
                                  1000)
  --excerpt-max-chars-total INTEGER
                                  Max total characters for excerpts  [default:
                                  60000]
  --max-age-seconds INTEGER       Max age in seconds before fetching live
                                  content (min 600)
  --timeout-seconds FLOAT         Timeout in seconds for fetching live content
  --disable-cache-fallback        Return error instead of stale cached content
  --location TEXT                 ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code for geo-
                                  targeted results (e.g. us, gb, de)
  --session-id TEXT               Session ID to group related search/extract
                                  calls
  --client-model TEXT             The model generating this request and
                                  consuming the results (e.g. claude-opus-4-7,
                                  gpt-5.4, gemini-3.1-pro)
  -o, --output PATH               Save results to file (JSON)
  --json                          Output as JSON
  --help                          Show this message and exit.
